MTD	mzTab-version	2.1.0-M
MTD	mzTab-ID	ST000956_AN001569
MTD	mzTab-profile	M+S
MTD	title	Determine metabolomics signatures important for the ability of Streptococus gallolyticus to promote colon cancer cell proliferation
MTD	description	HT29 cells were treated with Sg TX20005 stationary phase, Sg TX20005 exponential phase (negative control), and Sg TX20008 stationary phase (negative control), and media only (baseline control). The cells were washed and aliquoted. One aliquot was pelleted and stored at -80C for metabolomics analysis. DNA was also extracted from the other aliquot for DNA methylation studies.
